From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] chat : keep response-format grammars eager in qwen3-coder, deepseek and ministral3

The Qwen3-Coder parser (also used by Qwen3.5, Nemotron Nano 3, and Granite 4.2), the DeepSeek
parser, and the Ministral 3 parser mark their grammar lazy whenever tools are present without a
required tool choice, even when a response format constrains the whole reply. Their response-format
branch contains no tool-call trigger, and a lazy grammar keeps only the rules reachable from
triggers, so the response-format root comes out empty:

    root ::=
    space ::= | " " | "\n"{1,2} [ \t]{0,20}

and llama_sampler_init_grammar rejects it ("expecting newline or end at ::= ..."). Every
request with tools plus response_format and automatic tool choice fails. The generic
autoparser and the other specialized parsers that build a response-format branch (cohere2moe,
gemma4, gpt-oss, lfm2, minicpm5, minimax-m3) already guard laziness with !has_response_format;
this applies the same condition here. Parsers that ignore the response format entirely
(functionary-v3-2, gigachat-v3, kimi-k2, kimi-k3, ling3, muse-glimmer) are a separate gap that
this patch does not address.

Upstream report: not yet filed.

Validated against llama.cpp b11201 on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (CUDA 13.3): the
airtype-desktop-inference-sidecar tools_plus_structured_output_can_still_return_schema_json
suites fail on Qwen3.5 4B and Granite 4.2 3B without the patch and pass with it. The Ministral 3
hunk is the identical one-line condition, confirmed by printing the grammar
common_chat_templates_apply builds for a Ministral 3 template.

diff --git a/common/parsers/deepseek.cpp b/common/parsers/deepseek.cpp
index 9ca4bb3..1f23331 100644
--- a/common/parsers/deepseek.cpp
+++ b/common/parsers/deepseek.cpp
@@ -259,7 +259,7 @@ common_chat_params common_chat_params_init_deepseek_v3_2(const common_chat_templ
     data.parser = parser.save();
 
     if (include_grammar) {
-        data.grammar_lazy = has_tools && !require_tools;
+        data.grammar_lazy = !has_response_format && has_tools && !require_tools;
         data.grammar      = build_grammar([&](const common_grammar_builder & builder) {
             parser.build_grammar(builder, data.grammar_lazy);
         });
